I would say... descend, but carefully. Get yourself a nice base camp
down at level 10 or 11 that you can operate from, pile up lots of food
(soko, fishing pole, whatever) and then start moving down the dungeon.
Avoid being burdened. Sort your stash regularly, and make good use of
price ID/ shopkeeper ID. Clear each level before moving further.
Retreat at the first sign of real danger, and be very careful not to
step in any magic portals before you are ready (although you shouldn't
see those for at least another 5 levels.)

Sooner or later you'll find another altar. If you have to convert it,
first use a stethoscope or foo of enlightmenment/probing to check that
you have a good chance of converting it successfully. If you're not
ready, either get ready or keep looking. You're not ready to take on a
priest, BTW, and unless you happen to pick up a tame gug or jabberwock
I'd say it's unlikely you will be before finding a friendly altar
elsewhere.

Above all though, don't panic. Having a co-aligned altar for saccing
and blessing stuff is great, but you'll be just fine without one for a
long while yet. You can BUC-ID stuff in minetown, and you have some
neat weapons and decent stats. No need to do anything rash just yet.



